{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-14_14-15-46-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft; sed -n '1,45p' update.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"The AddVoter receipt answered the question in the affirmative on both halves: the added server appears as a Voter rather than a staging server, and on a single-voter cluster that immediately removes the cluster's ability to commit, to elect, and to undo the change through the same API, while the identical change on a three-voter cluster is harmless. This submission records that account with the documented bootstrap workflow it interacts with, promotes the two knowledge entries the account rests on, and keeps the out-of-band recovery path and the stale-documentation reading visible as counterevidence rather than letting the finding stand unqualified.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"api_bootstrap_workflow\",\n      \"file\": \"api.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 240,\n      \"end_line\": 247,\n      \"kind\": \"document_statement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"api_recover_cluster_contract\",\n      \"file\": \"api.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 290,\n      \"end_line\": 325,\n      \"kind\": \"document_statement\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"investigations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7c32ee99c0e474f8b48309e4800bc32-question-0\",\n      \"disposition\": \"explained\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sources_duplicate_guard\": [],\n    {\n      \"id\": \"api_bootstrap_workflow\",\n      \"file\": \"api.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 240,\n      \"end_line\": 247,\n      \"kind\": \"document_statement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"api_recover_cluster_contract\",\n      \"file\": \"api.go\",\n      \"start_line\": 290,\n      \"end_line\": 325,\n      \"kind\": \"document_statement\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@addvoter_installs_voter\",\n      \"kind\": \"behavior\",\n      \"statement\": \"The AddVoter configuration change installs the requested server with Suffrage Voter in one step: nextConfiguration's AddVoter branch builds the new Server with Suffrage Voter, the resulting configuration is appended as a single LogConfiguration (or the deprecated remove-peer entry below protocol version 2), and the leader applies it to the commitment and to replication immediately after dispatching it. Nothing in the captured path creates a Staging server or defers promotion, despite the AddVoter comment that describes the server as added for staging and promoted by the leader once it is ready.\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
